From: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: restore AN7563 TX fragment mapping

The original AN7563 transmit path maps both the skb head and its page
fragments with dma_map_single().  The unified path changed fragments to
skb_frag_dma_map() and consequently unmaps them with dma_unmap_page().

AN7563 runs without high memory and skb_frag_address() is valid for its
TX fragments.  Restore the original mapping method on AN7563 while
retaining page-based fragment mapping on the other SoCs.

Signed-off-by: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -7483,19 +7483,25 @@ static netdev_tx_t __airoha_dev_xmit
 	while (i < nr_frags) {
 		struct airoha_qdma_desc *desc = &q->desc[index];
-		bool map_page = i > 0;
+		bool map_page = i > 0 &&
+				!airoha_is(qdma->eth, airoha_an7563);
 		dma_addr_t addr;
 		u32 val;
 
-		if (map_page) {
+		if (i > 0) {
 			skb_frag_t *frag = &skb_shinfo(skb)->frags[i - 1];
 
 			len = skb_frag_size(frag);
-			addr = skb_frag_dma_map(netdev->dev.parent, frag, 0,
-						len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+			if (map_page)
+				addr = skb_frag_dma_map(netdev->dev.parent, frag, 0,
+							len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+			else
+				addr = dma_map_single(netdev->dev.parent,
+						      skb_frag_address(frag), len,
+						      DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 		} else {
 			len = skb_headlen(skb);
 			addr = dma_map_single(netdev->dev.parent, skb->data, len,
 					      DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 		}
 		if (unlikely(dma_mapping_error(netdev->dev.parent, addr)))
 			goto error_unmap;
-- 
